`WKWebView` and `WKNavigationDelegate` are `@MainActor`-isolated in current SDKs. `captureFrameAndOrigin` and `FakeWKNavigationDelegate` aren't annotated. The callers in `WKUIHandlerTests` happen to be `@MainActor`, and the `WebEngineTests` target doesn't enable strict concurrency, so this builds today with warnings at most. It will turn into errors once the test target adopts the strict-concurrency settings the production targets already use (Package.swift). Other helpers in this folder, such as `DefaultTestDependencies.swift`, are already marked `@MainActor`.

